WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.530
- How are you doing?
- Good, doing well.

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:02.450
- Yeah? Okay.

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.610
So wait, we were talking
about getting away with stuff.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.190
Were you the kid that ever
got away with anything,

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.330
like really good?

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:08.670
- Very much, I think I still am.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.870
- Breaking rules?
- Yeah.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:10.815
- I like it.

00:00:10.815 --> 00:00:13.270
- I used to do this thing,
- For fun.

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:16.630
where if I was late, it only worked twice,

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:18.650
but when I was a kid and I was late,

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.393
I would call home and
when my mom picked up,

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.620
she would go, "Hello,"
and I'd go, "I got it."

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:25.500
- Oh, my-
- And she would think

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.590
I was home,

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:28.940
and I would just hang up.
- That's so clever.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.650
- And then stay out for another
two hours, and come home.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:32.483
She thought I was...

00:00:32.483 --> 00:00:34.608
All she had to do was like
look down the hallway.

00:00:34.608 --> 00:00:35.630
(audience laughing)

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:36.840
But, yeah. Yeah.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:37.673
I was a brave-

00:00:37.673 --> 00:00:39.840
- Now here's the thing-
- not smart child. (laughs)

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.590
- No, you are smart. That's very clever.

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:42.950
I feel like you deserved that.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:44.660
- I've always wanted to put it in a movie.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.690
It'll work.
- Yes.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:47.670
- Oh, my gosh.
(Bobby laughs)

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.810
I'm totally gonna check my
kids' rooms when they're older.

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:52.310
Okay, so I wanna know,
'cause you've been on SNL,

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:54.120
I wanna know what are
your favorite characters

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.060
that you've ever gotten to play?

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.890
- Wow. I mean all of...

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.250
Anytime I was on camera at SNL,

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:03.195
15-year-old me was
extremely excited about it,

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:04.630
- Yeah.
- but I mean like...

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:07.750
Gosh, they all change.
- It is a certain energy.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.440
I've been there, just
performing and stuff.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:10.610
- Have you hosted?

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:11.443
- No, I don't know.

00:01:11.443 --> 00:01:12.960
- You have to, you
would be a perfect host.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.568
- It's such a commitment.

00:01:14.568 --> 00:01:16.811
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:01:16.811 --> 00:01:19.200
I was actually in New York
when Blake Shelton hosted

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.280
'cause-
- Ooh, I was there for that.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.210
He was great.
- I know.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:22.330
But it is a commitment.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:23.350
Y'all work all week.

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:24.183
People don't get it.

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:25.620
It's not just Saturday night.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.461
- No, it's a lot of work.
- It's like all week long.

00:01:27.461 --> 00:01:28.294
Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:28.294 --> 00:01:30.820
I feel like you are someone
that would excel at it though

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.020
- Oh, really?
- 'cause you're hilarious.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.160
I feel like you would let them have fun,

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.260
and have a good time.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:37.500
- Oh, I would definitely lean in

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.833
and have a good time.
- Yeah.

00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:39.790
I feel like you would be a great host.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:41.756
I wanna see it.
- Okay.

00:01:41.756 --> 00:01:43.000
(audience cheers and applauds)
(Bobby laughs)

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:43.833
- I love that.

00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:45.790
Thank you. Thank you.
- Blake was great.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:48.534
- Do you remember your very
first time that you were on SNL?

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:50.200
'Cause you said you were
15-year-old, so it's freaking out.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.830
So, what was like your
first, do you remember?

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:54.040
- Yeah, I totally remember.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:55.750
It was like Space Camp.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:56.620
- Aw.
- It was nuts.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:59.530
I mean, the first episode
was the only one I enjoyed

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:00.367
because I was like,
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:01.820
"I'm here. I can't believe it."

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.422
And then there was a job after that.

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:04.255
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:04.255 --> 00:02:05.088
- Yeah, no.

00:02:05.088 --> 00:02:07.790
I definitely, in between two scenes

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:12.180
in my first episode, ran
full speed across the studio

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.530
and changed really fast
'cause we're on live TV,

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.640
and then I had like a minute and a half.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:17.824
And I was just standing-
- But you think

00:02:17.824 --> 00:02:18.657
a quick change-
- there going like,

00:02:18.657 --> 00:02:22.168
"Yeah, yeah. I guess I'm
very excited to be here."

00:02:22.168 --> 00:02:23.190
(both laughing)
- Oh, my God.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:24.600
You had your pocket protector on.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.940
- Yeah, I was very...
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:27.457
My old SNL book.

00:02:27.457 --> 00:02:28.680
(both laughing)
- Love it.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.780
So wait, do you remember
your first time performing

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:31.710
in front of a crowd?

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.990
Were you nervous or did you feel at home?

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.350
- I don't think I was nervous,

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:37.081
and maybe that's why I'm here now.

00:02:37.081 --> 00:02:38.440
- Me neither.
- I think I'm like Santa Claus

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:40.290
when I was a kid in school,
- Yeah.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:43.300
like in third grade and
remember being like, yeah.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.190
- The kid never gets to play Santa Claus.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:46.250
That's awesome.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:48.280
- Yeah, I wasn't even chubby then,

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:49.309
like I am now.
- No, I just mean

00:02:49.309 --> 00:02:50.570
(audience laughing)
like most kids have to be

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.370
like elves or something.
You got to be the big man.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:53.203
- That's awesome.
- I got to be Santa.

00:02:53.203 --> 00:02:54.810
Yeah. I was like the
only one who said yes,

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.255
and I had a beard (Kelly
laughs) when I was four.

00:02:57.255 --> 00:02:58.500
(Bobby laughs)
- So, it fit.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.550
I love it.
- Yeah.

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:02.217
And then every year, for nine
years at SNL, it was like,

00:03:02.217 --> 00:03:03.300
"It's December, you gotta put on

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.580
a Santa Claus costume five times
a week for the next month."

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:07.570
- Oh, my God.
(Bobby laughs)

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:08.770
That's awesome, though.

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:11.220
Wait, I love that your first
time wasn't scary, though.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.060
A lot of times when performers
would say they were terrified

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:15.300
and I was like, that's
why I feel like I'm here.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.133
I enjoyed it.

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:17.860
Like my first time was on stage.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:19.560
It kind of felt like home away from home.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.003
- Yeah. I remember like,

00:03:22.612 --> 00:03:23.590
I was like the big finish at the end,

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:25.500
was putting on this Santa Claus jacket,

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.840
and it was inside out, and they did it,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.467
they handed it to me wrong.
- Oh.

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:33.150
- And I remember making
some joke about it,

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:36.150
and then putting it on,
and it got a big laugh-

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.387
- And then a star was born.
- Being like,

00:03:37.387 --> 00:03:38.760
"Well, that's how it's done, people."

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:42.010
- Yeah. (laughs)
Like, at the age of three.

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:43.468
- Already clever and funny.
(Bobby laughs)

00:03:43.468 --> 00:03:44.416
(audience applauding)
I love it.

00:03:44.416 --> 00:03:45.384
(audience applauding)
I love it.

00:03:45.384 --> 00:03:46.500
- So, congrats on season
two of "Mr. Mayor".

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:47.570
- Thanks. Thank you.
- That's amazing.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:48.700
- For people that haven't seen it yet,

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:49.850
what is the show kind of about?

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:51.080
Who's your character?

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.550
- I play Jayden Kwapis on "Mr. Mayor".

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:56.750
It's a show about, Ted
Danson plays the mayor of LA,

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:57.583
Mayor Bremer.

00:03:57.583 --> 00:03:58.650
Thanks.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.570
And he's kind of just
trying to prove to himself

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:03.670
that he could still do
it and to his daughter.

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:06.130
And maybe he shouldn't
be, or maybe he should.

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:07.050
We'll see.
(Bobby laughs)

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.280
- I love that, the suspense.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:11.840
You also have a podcast, and
it's "Celebrity Sightings",

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:12.673
right?
- Yeah.

00:04:12.673 --> 00:04:15.050
So, what is your coolest
celebrity sighting or weirdest?

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:16.630
I'll take any.

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:18.140
- Oh, wow.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:19.440
I do have a podcast
called "Celebrity Sighting

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:20.310
with Jonathan Biting".

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.290
I play a character, a
hundred-year-old man.

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:23.723
That's him.

00:04:23.723 --> 00:04:24.990
(Kelly laughs)
I play a hundred-year-old man

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.120
named Jonathan Biting, who hides in bushes

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.716
and takes pictures of celebrities.

00:04:28.716 --> 00:04:30.080
(both laughing)

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.300
My weirdest celebrity encounter,

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.130
gosh, I wish I had a better one,

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:35.580
like just regularly on the street.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.330
I did, I ran into Anthony Daniels,

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:38.560
the guy who plays C-3PO,

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:39.690
- Yeah.
- on the street.

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:41.910
And I recognized him, and
I think he was shocked

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:43.500
that I recognized him out of costume,

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:44.333
I think.
- Yeah.

00:04:44.333 --> 00:04:45.166
- But he was walking

00:04:45.166 --> 00:04:47.150
like C-3PO.
(audience laughing)

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:48.334
He was.

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:49.167
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:50.000
I think-

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.576
- "Maybe they'll know who I am."

00:04:51.576 --> 00:04:52.409
(everyone laughing)

00:04:52.409 --> 00:04:57.340
- I think, by far, the weirdest
one was definitely at SNL.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:00.060
I was walking down the
hallway in a moose costume

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.770
with a moose head.
- As you do.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:03.253
- As you do.

00:05:03.253 --> 00:05:04.800
And Sarah Palin walked by me.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.380
- Yeah.
- I never met her before.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:08.410
Never said a word to her.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.310
Her first words to me, as she walked by,

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:11.470
she never looked at me,

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:12.607
she just went,
(imitates gun cocking)

00:05:12.607 --> 00:05:14.070
"Moose!"

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.698
- Oh, my God.
(audience laughing)

00:05:15.698 --> 00:05:18.690
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:21.880
That's actually fantastic.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:22.960
Wait.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:24.160
- Super weird.
(Bobby laughs)

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:25.330
She was ready to go hunting.
- Yeah.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:26.820
She had it ready.
- Oh, my God.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.393
- It feel like not her first
moose that she's encountered.

00:05:29.393 --> 00:05:30.226
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:05:30.226 --> 00:05:31.570
- Not in Alaska. No.

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:33.681
- No, no, definitely inside "30 Rock".

00:05:33.681 --> 00:05:37.792
- Huh?
(both laughing)

